note The io-source crate: reading the source tree. walk lists and reads every text file under the root the way design section 7 says (the ignore crate, so .gitignore and hidden directories are respected even outside a git repo; files over 4 MiB or with a NUL byte in their first 1 KiB skipped as binary), and every text it hands out is a Contents, tab-expanded once so display, hashing and columns agree. It also carries each file's modification time, which the GUI's watcher thread polls to notice an edit. It reads and never writes.

